# Type labels (Projects + Insights)

On `.projects-page`, `.project-detail`, `.insights-page`, `.insight-detail`:

1. **No fill** — no border, background, or capsule padding on type labels.
2. **Font** — FK Grotesk Mono Medium (`var(--font-label)`, weight `500`). CSS: `--font-type-label`.
3. **Size** — shared `--type-chip-font` (current size, −3% recipe). Same everywhere: featured, cards, Related, case hero tag.
4. **Color** — gray (`--type-label-color`).
5. **Card / lead title + description** on light surfaces — **black** (`#0a0a0a`). Type label stays gray. Dark detail Related stays white title/desc.

Applies to `.project-type-chip`, `.insight-chip`, `.project-case-demo__tag`.

Filter involvement pills are separate UI — not this recipe.

# Filter / Related / home cards (all breakpoints)

**Scope:** `.project-window__meta--stack`, `.insight-showcase__meta`.

Stack in three rows (full width). **Projects and Insights share the same tokens** (`:root`):

- `--card-meta-row-gap` — title ↔ description
- `--card-meta-type-gap` — description ↔ type label
- `--card-meta-desc-size` / `--card-meta-desc-lh` (+ mobile variants)
- Title: `--project-meta-title-size` / `--project-meta-title-weight` (same on both)

1. **Title** (black on light)
2. **Description** (black on light)
3. **Type label** (gray, left-aligned; same Mono / size / tracking as all type labels)

Do **not** put the type label on the same row as the title.
Do **not** give Insights a different letter-spacing or size than Projects for these cards.

# Featured leads (Projects + Insights)

**Scope:** `.project-featured__meta`, `.insights-lead__meta`.

Restore / keep the prior recipe (not the three-row card stack):

- **Desktop:** type label end-aligned; description left-aligned with centered-nav inset; title→desc **5.5vw**; desc→tag **10vw**.
- **Mobile ≤800px:** title ≤65% | type end-aligned; description full width on the next row.

# Exception — project detail case hero

`.project-case-demo__hero-copy` keeps the existing overlay recipe. Do **not** restack it unless the user explicitly asks.
